% path_sandbox — decide whether the agent is allowed to read a path

# Module: path_sandbox

## Intent

The CoPrompt agent reads the team's codebase to understand it. It must never
read anything outside that codebase: not `../../.ssh/id_rsa`, not `/etc/passwd`,
not a symlink that quietly points out of the tree.

This module is that boundary. It is the only thing standing between "the agent
can read your repo" and "the agent can read your laptop", so it is written as a
prompt with its forbidden outcomes stated first, and it fails closed.

Pure decision logic over paths. It does not open files and does not read
contents.

## Interface

```python
class SandboxViolation(Exception):
    """Raised when a path is not inside the sandbox root."""


def resolve(root: str | Path, candidate: str) -> Path:
    ...

def is_inside(root: str | Path, candidate: str) -> bool:
    ...
```

- `root` is the repository root. It is trusted.
- `candidate` is a path from the agent, expected to be relative to `root`.
- `resolve` returns the absolute, fully-resolved `Path` when the candidate is
  inside the sandbox, and raises `SandboxViolation` otherwise.
- `is_inside` answers the same question without raising.

Both must resolve symlinks before deciding, so a link inside the tree that
points outside it is rejected on where it *lands*, not where it sits.

## MUST NOT

These come first because they are the point of the module.

- MUST NOT accept a path that escapes the root by traversal:
  `../secrets`, `a/../../secrets`, `./../../secrets`.
- MUST NOT accept an absolute path outside the root, such as `/etc/passwd` or
  `/Users/someone/.ssh/id_rsa`, even when it exists.
- MUST NOT accept a path whose resolved location is outside the root, even when
  every textual component looks harmless -- a symlink must be followed before
  the decision is made.
- MUST NOT accept a path that merely shares a prefix with the root as a string:
  if root is `/home/app/repo`, then `/home/app/repo-secrets/x` is OUTSIDE and
  must be rejected. String prefix comparison is not containment.
- MUST NOT accept a candidate whose first path component begins with `~`
  (`~/.ssh/id_rsa`, `~root/.ssh/id_rsa`). REJECT it outright with
  `SandboxViolation`. Do not expand it, and do not fall back to treating it as
  an ordinary relative name -- joining `~/.ssh/id_rsa` onto the root lands
  inside the sandbox and silently allows a path the caller clearly did not
  intend as a literal directory named `~`.
- MUST NOT accept a null byte anywhere in the candidate.
- MUST NOT perform any I/O beyond what path resolution requires. It never opens
  or reads a file.

## MUST

- MUST accept an ordinary relative path inside the root: `app/main.py`,
  `./app/main.py`, `prompts/x.prompt`.
- MUST accept an absolute path that is genuinely inside the root.
- MUST accept the root itself, and `.`, and `""` (both meaning the root).
- MUST accept a path that traverses upward but lands back inside:
  `app/../app/main.py`.
- MUST accept a path that does not exist yet, as long as its resolved location
  is inside the root -- the module answers "may this be read", not "does this
  exist".
- MUST return an absolute, resolved `Path` from `resolve`.
- MUST make `is_inside` return exactly `not raises` for the same input, so the
  two functions can never disagree.
- MUST raise `SandboxViolation`, not a bare `ValueError`, so callers can
  distinguish a security refusal from a bad argument.

## Examples

```python
resolve("/repo", "app/main.py")        # -> Path("/repo/app/main.py")
resolve("/repo", "./app/../app/x.py")  # -> Path("/repo/app/x.py")
resolve("/repo", "")                   # -> Path("/repo")

resolve("/repo", "../secrets")         # raises SandboxViolation
resolve("/repo", "/etc/passwd")        # raises SandboxViolation
resolve("/repo", "a/../../secrets")    # raises SandboxViolation
resolve("/repo", "~/.ssh/id_rsa")      # raises SandboxViolation

is_inside("/repo", "app/main.py")      # -> True
is_inside("/repo", "../secrets")       # -> False

# Prefix is not containment:
is_inside("/home/app/repo", "/home/app/repo-secrets/x")   # -> False
```

## Done when

- Every example above returns exactly the stated result.
- A symlink inside the root pointing outside it is rejected.
- The module has no imports beyond the standard library.
